# Round q38head2: Qwen3.8's MTP draft with its reduced head read in place (q8_0_gemv_ids, q8_0_gemv_ids_mcol: the
# target's `output` rows of the list through the head's map, no gathered copy) and a list picked from a Korean chat
# curve, against the full head, same binary, the shipped default otherwise (residency, the MTP draft and host
# streaming unset: mid-p121-s1, mtp, on).
# The list: $BLOOMERY_DATA/qwen4exp/heldout/mtp-head-rows-kohangul-65536.txt (md5 7c07cfb143e0...), built by
# tools/ref/draft-vocab.py's run() over corpus-code.ids, corpus-threads.ids and corpus-korean.ids (the q38head
# lists' sources plus this repo's Korean docs), the ten `learn` prompts of tools/ref/data/d2-prompts-ko.tsv as the
# serve path renders them (bloomery-serve /apply-template on the target's header, ik-idxkey's llama-tokenize, 774
# ids) and the full head's greedy replies to them (2,742 ids), every Hangul token of the vocabulary kept (6,807),
# filled to 65,536 with the lowest ids (31,324). The ten `held` prompts are in no source. Held-out coverage:
# corpus-prose.ids 0.99197 (the q38head 65,536 list 0.99268); the held Korean chat replies' 2,801 ids 0.9861
# (q38head's 65,536 list 0.6887).
#
# [derived] Term: the head bytes a window. The full head is 248,320 rows x 2,720 B = 675.43 MB a walk, three walks
# a window, 2.026 GB; the list reads 65,536 x 2,720 = 178.26 MB a walk and saves 1.492 GB a window, 2.19-2.43 ms at
# 615-680 GB/s (the gathered copy measured -2.55 ms at P 4096 beside a +0.04..+0.12 ms card-expert move, so up to
# 2.67 ms). The in-place read is the gathered copy's bytes and sectors (a row's 2,560 code bytes are 20 whole
# 128-B lines at id x 2,560, its 160 scale bytes 5 whole 32-B sectors at id x 160) and occupancy (m = 1: 40 regs,
# 6 blocks/SM, q8_0_gemv's; m > 1: 80 regs against q8_0_gemv_mcol's 72, both 3 blocks/SM), plus a 4-B id a row:
# +-0.1 ms a walk, +-0.3 ms a window. The plan is the full head's, byte for byte (the map is 248,320 x 4 B either
# way; card_experts 11680, P 121, card_bytes 2846073004 in every functional load below), so no card-expert term.
# Windows 38.35 ms (P 512) and 37.11 ms (P 4096), rig-log 10-01#q38hol-ab: -1.89..-2.97 ms, -4.9..-7.7 % (P 512),
# -5.1..-8.0 % (P 4096). Band -8..-4.5.
#
# Functional runs (this tree's binary, --place a, A6000, ctx 4352, n 300, untimed, BLOOMERY_MTP_WINDOWS=1): prose
# P 512 prints one tokens line under the full head, the q38head 65,536 and 98,304 lists and this list, and one mtp
# summary kept=[20, 15, 10, 55]; the held Korean prompt ko-02 prints the full head's tokens and kept=[42, 39, 12, 36]
# under this list. The A/B's own load (--arm <prose 512> --arm <prose 4096> -n 96 --ctx 4352, one load a head,
# default residency) prints one tokens line per P under both heads; at P 512 both keep [0, 3, 2, 21] (26 passes),
# at P 4096 the full head [4, 6, 4, 17] (31 passes) and the list [5, 6, 5, 16] (32). So tok/s moves by the pass
# time alone at P 512, +5.2..+8.7 % [derived], and at P 4096 with E(4) 3.097 -> 3.000 beside it, +2.0..+5.4 %
# [derived]. (Under the
# q38head 65,536 list ko-02 kept [151, 27, 14, 13] and its tokens part from the full head's at generated token 102;
# under BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=off the same prompt keeps [88, 36, 13, 25] against [47, 24, 20, 36] and prints the full
# head's tokens: the running residency counts by pass, the lever's doc.)
# Korean chat [derived, no run]: the head's saving is bytes a walk and does not depend on the text, so the prose
# rows time it; the Korean cost is the lost positions a window. Net ms a window = the saving a walk x 3 - the lost
# positions a window x the cost a position:
#   saving a walk: this run's prose rows (until then the gathered copy's -2.55 ms a window at P 4096, rig-log
#     10-01#q38head-ab, 0.85 ms a walk);
#   lost positions a window: 0.000 on ko-02 (115 windows of the full head's log, tools/flow/q38width.py's head
#     cut against this list; the q38head 65,536 list loses 0.522), 0.032 over the ten held prompts (1,135 windows);
#   cost a position: the full head's window over its positions on that log, 39.36 / 2.174 = 18.11 ms (ko-02),
#     39.36 / 2.464 = 15.97 ms (ten prompts), q38width's step 17.49 + 3 x 7.29 ms;
#   so ko-02 +2.55 ms a window (tok/s +6.9 %), the ten prompts +2.04 ms (+5.5 %), at the gathered copy's saving.
# The ko-02 ids (the serve path's template, 77 ids): $BLOOMERY_DATA/qwen4exp/heldout/ko-02.ids, a note only.
# The term is read from each arm's `time pass` rows of kind=mtp, warm passes left out, as q38head-ab's.
# Runner (lead, from the q38head2 tree, the full output to a file first):
# BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/q38head2-ab.card BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4352' BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=6
# just depth-gpu-qwen4exp prose:512 prose:512@BLOOMERY_MTP_HEAD_ROWS=/root/bloomery-data/qwen4exp/heldout/mtp-head-rows-kohangul-65536.txt
#   prose:4096 prose:4096@BLOOMERY_MTP_HEAD_ROWS=/root/bloomery-data/qwen4exp/heldout/mtp-head-rows-kohangul-65536.txt
# (`depth-qwen3moe.sh --parse-arms`: two load groups, each its two P in one process, rotated.)
# Rounds: sd 1.0 %, q38seed-mtp's same-binary MTP pairs, as q38head-ab's; 6 rounds give h 1.3 %, under the band's
# edge 4.5.
# Wall [derived]: 2 load groups x 6 rounds = 12 Qwen3.8 loads with the draft (19-58 s each in the functional runs),
# the two prompts (0.5 + 3.4 s) and 2 x 96 tokens a load (3-5 s): 5-13 min, with the build and the witness blocks
# 7-16 min.
kind: ab
question: does Qwen3.8's reduced MTP head read in place (the kohangul-65536 list) shorten the drafted pass by the
  head bytes it stops reading, with the plan, the tokens and the kept counts the full head's?
term: ms per drafted pass (time pass rows, kind=mtp, warm left out) @ n=96, prose:512 and prose:4096, ctx 4352,
  A6000, plan a, residency, draft and host streaming unset (mtp),
  BLOOMERY_MTP_HEAD_ROWS=heldout/mtp-head-rows-kohangul-65536.txt against unset, same binary, paired by round
unit: %
predict: -8..-4.5
rounds: 6
sd: 1.0 % q38seed-mtp's same-binary MTP pairs (rig-log 09-30#q38seed-ab, 6 rounds, +-1.3 % / +-0.9 %)
condition: one binary, every arm of a P in one lease, a fresh process per load group, the host set and the PLE
  table warm, no [cpu-busy] or [other-busy] row; both arms' plan lines card_experts 11680 and residency unset
  mid-p121-s1, both load draft lines card_bytes 2846073004 (head=full and head=rows=65536); at each P both arms
  print one tokens line, at P 512 one mtp summary kept list ([0, 3, 2, 21]) and at P 4096 the functional load's
  ([4, 6, 4, 17] and [5, 6, 5, 16]); every load finds its host set resident (the functional
  loads that ran beside another session's 180 GB gate ended on `SwapMachine`'s `is not host-resident`
  refusal; the lease's quiet machine is the guard, and such a load voids its round); each arm's mtp summary
  E(4) and tok/s read beside its pass time
decide-in: the head is on the pass's path at its bytes and reads in place for free: put the measured saving a
  walk into the Korean chat line above, then propose the list as the Qwen3.8 MTP default with these rows, its
  tok/s and E(4) beside them and the Korean line [derived]
decide-below: the pass shortened less than the bytes: one nsys window of a drafted pass, q8_0_gemv_ids and
  q8_0_gemv_ids_mcol against the full head's q8_0_gemv and q8_0_gemv_mcol at 615-680 GB/s, before any change
decide-above: the pass shortened by more than the head's bytes: check the condition first (a tokens line or a
  kept list that differs between the arms moves the residency's passes); with both equal, read the arms' host
  slots and residency pass records before proposing a default
